   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="transliteration" xml:lang="pal">
            <pb xml:id="pb-1r-trl" facs="berkeley:recid:85282-65.recto_ii.jpg/full/full/0/default.jpg"/>
            <ab xml:id="MP0070_trl-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trl-p1-l1"/>[wh]ʾk ʾnd ḤS wšpṭk'
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trl-p1-l2"/>[h]cdl Y QDM ck' MNW
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trl-p1-l3"/>ʾdybʾṭkʾl ʾwb-š wylʾsṭ'
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trl-p1-l4"/>W npšṭ' YKʿYMWNyṭ MN plhw'
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trl-p1-l5"/>MKḆLWNty W bnd Y ẔNH
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trl-p1-l6"/>ʾdybʾṭkʾl kʾlw(ʾn)yk PWN gw(k)ʾdy-mwdlyhʾ
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trl-p1-l7"/>Y ʾsp̄pʾṭ Y kṭksp̄ṭ'
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trl-p1-l8"/>ḤṬYMWNṭ
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="transcription" xml:lang="pal">
            <ab xml:id="MP0070_trc-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trc-p1-l1"/>[wah]āg and may wišuftag
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trc-p1-l2"/>(a)zēr ī abar čak kē ēn
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trc-p1-l3"/>ayādgār awi-š wirāst
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trc-p1-l4"/>ud nibišt ēstēd az Farrox
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trc-p1-l5"/>padīrēd ud band ī ēn
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trc-p1-l6"/>ayādgār kārawānīg pad gugāy-muhrīhā
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trc-p1-l7"/>ī Aspbād ī *kadagsbed
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trc-p1-l8"/>āwišt
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
            <ab xml:id="MP0070_trans-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trans-p1-l1"/>[Val]ue of as much wine was spilled
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trans-p1-l2"/>when presenting the čak [be]low on which this
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trans-p1-l3"/>ayādgār is established
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trans-p1-l4"/>and written, from Farrox
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trans-p1-l5"/>he receives. And the tie of this
               <lb n="6-8" xml:id="trans-p1-l6-8"/>ayādgār was sealed by the caravaneer (leader of the caravan) with the witnesses' seals of Aspbād, the *caretaker.
            </ab>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
</TEI>